From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LvglLib: Fix the circle mask of a large radius, from LVGL
 v9.6.0

LvglLib builds LVGL v9.5.0, whose circ_calc_aa4() computes the
anti-aliased edge of a rounded mask: the points of one eighth of the
circle, the point at 45 degrees, the other eighth mirrored, then an
index of the points by row. The point at 45 degrees is
radius * 723 / 1024, a little short of radius / sqrt(2): for some radii
from 922 px on it falls on an earlier row than the last point of the
first eighth. The index takes the points of a row while their row
equals y, stops at that point for good, and goes on writing rows past
the 6 * radius + 6 bytes of the buffer until it faults.

The orbs of the wallpaper (0011) have a radius of 52, 58 and 62% of the
screen height: at 1080 px at most 669 px, at 1620 px 842, 939 and
1004 px. With the 2880 x 1620 framebuffer of the ThinkPad W541 the setup
stopped on a page fault in circ_calc_aa4(), for the orb of 939 px,
before it drew anything: a black screen, at any UI scale.

LVGL v9.6.0 fixes the index: a row takes the points up to its row, so
that a point that comes late ends the row before it (commit
f9c059715db7, "fix(draw): resolve infinite loop and out-of-bounds access
in circular mask cache calculation (#9864)", by Kreedb). Take the same
change into the LVGL submodule of LvglLib: the file is then the one of
that commit.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 Library/LvglLib/lvgl/src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c b/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c
index f5e8c5aea..68f368c29 100644
--- a/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c
+++ b/Library/LvglLib/lvgl/src/draw/sw/lv_draw_sw_mask.c
@@ -1209,7 +1209,7 @@ static void circ_calc_aa4(lv_draw_sw_mask_radius_circle_dsc_t * c, int32_t radiu
     while(i < cir_size) {
         c->opa_start_on_y[y] = i;
         c->x_start_on_y[y] = cir_x[i];
-        for(; i < (int32_t)cir_size && cir_y[i] == y; i++) {
+        for(; i < (int32_t)cir_size && cir_y[i] <= y; i++) {
             c->x_start_on_y[y] = LV_MIN(c->x_start_on_y[y], cir_x[i]);
         }
         y++;
